<div class=3D"flex h-full w-full items-center justify-center">
    <div class=3D"w-4/5 flex flex-col my-20">
        <div class=3D"mb-8">
            <h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-creablue">Help - Frequently=
 Asked Questions</h2>
            <p>If you have more questions, you can download our detailed <a=
 href=3D"https://crea2-dev.azurewebsites.net/Help" about=3D"_blank">handboo=
k</a> or <a href=3D"mailto:crea_project@proton.me">contact us</a> directly<=
/p>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"mb-8">
            <h3 class=3D"text-xl font-bold mb-4">General</h3>
            <div class=3D"flex">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center full-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>What is CREA ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button"><i class=3D"fa-solid fa-min=
us" aria-hidden=3D"true"></i></button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mt-4">
                        CREA2 is an innovative project that builds on previ=
ous work to help people and businesses resolve disputes using advanced tech=
nology. It introduces AI-driven tools and game-theoretical algorithms to gu=
ide users through the dispute resolution process step-by-step. CREA2 aims t=
o simplify access to justice across different EU countries by creating a co=
mmon set of rights and leveraging smart technologies like blockchain and AI=
 chatbots. This platform is designed to make resolving civil disputes easie=
r, more efficient, and fairer for everyone involved.

                        During a dispute resolution on CREA2, you are requi=
red to invite the different parties involved in the dispute, then add the g=
oods and their valuations. Once this information is provided, you will be a=
ble to set your preference for each of the goods. Finally, the resolution a=
lgorithm will propose an equitable distribution of the goods.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"mb-8">
            <h3 class=3D"text-xl font-bold mb-4">User account</h3>
            <div class=3D"flex flex-col">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>How do I create an account on CREA ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        To create an account on CREA2, click on the "GO to =
CREA Solution" button. You will be asked to login to your account. To regis=
ter as a new user, click on =E2=80=9CCreate your account now=E2=80=9D under=
neath the login form.

                        Fill in your personal details, such as your first n=
ame, last name, email address, and password. Follow the on-screen instructi=
ons to complete the registration process.

                        Once registered, you can log in with your e-mail ad=
ress and your password and start using the platform.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>I've received an e-mail to join a dispute. How =
do I accept the invitation ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        If you have received an email invitation to join a =
dispute, open the email and click on the provided link. This will take you =
to the CREA2 platform.

                        If you already have an account, log in using your c=
redentials. If you don't have an account, you'll need to create one by foll=
owing the registration process (See previous question).

                        Once logged in, you will be able to view and accept=
 the dispute invitation.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>Can I edit my account information on CREA ?</h3=
>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        Yes, you can edit your account information on CREA2=
.
                        To do this, log in to your account and navigate to =
the user management section by clicking on your profile or account settings=
.
                        Here, you can update your personal information, suc=
h as your first name and last name, by clicking the "Edit" button, making t=
he necessary changes, and then saving them. You can also change your passwo=
rd in this section.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>Can I delete my account on CREA ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        Yes, you can delete your account on CREA2. However,=
 please note that your account cannot be deleted during an on-going dispute=
.

                        To delete your account, go to the user management s=
ection of your profile. Click on the "Delete Account" button, which will op=
en a confirmation dialog. Read the warning message carefully, and if you ar=
e sure you want to proceed, click the "Confirm" button to permanently delet=
e your account. Note that this action is irreversible and will remove all y=
our data from the system.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"mb-8">
            <h3 class=3D"text-xl font-bold mb-4">Disputes</h3>
            <div class=3D"flex flex-col">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>What is a dispute ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        A dispute on CREA2 refers to a procedure between ag=
ents that aims to solve a legal conflict on asset division. CREA2 facilitat=
es the resolution process by guiding users through a structured, step-by-st=
ep approach using advanced AI-driven tools and innovative game-theoretical =
algorithms. This ensures that all parties can reach a fair and efficient re=
solution, tailored to their specific needs and preferences.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>What are the resolution methods "Bids"and "Rate=
s" ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        The resolution methods "Bids" and "Rates" are two w=
ays to express preferences for resolving a dispute on CREA2:

                        Bids Method: Users are given a virtual amount of mo=
ney to distribute across the goods involved in the dispute, expressing thei=
r preferences through monetary bids.
                        Rates Method: Users rate each good on a 5-star scal=
e, indicating their preferences by assigning a value from 1 to 5 stars.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>How do I invite agents to join a dispute ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        To invite agents to join a dispute on CREA2, follow=
 these steps:

                        Start by setting up your dispute and navigate to th=
e agent section.
                        Click the "Add New Agent" button.
                        Fill in the required details for the agent, includi=
ng their name, email address, share of entitlement, and optional role.
                        Submit the information to add the agent to your dis=
pute.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>How can i add goods to a dispute ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        To add goods to a dispute on CREA2, follow these st=
eps:

                        During the dispute setup process, navigate to the g=
oods section.
                        Click the "Add New Good" button.
                        Enter the necessary details for the good, such as t=
he name, estimated value, and optional indivisibility.
                        Submit the information to add the good to your disp=
ute.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>What are agent preferences ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        Agent preferences on CREA2 refer to the individual =
priorities or utilities that agents assign to the goods involved in the dis=
pute. These preferences are set using the method chosen in the initial disp=
ute setup (either "Bids" or "Rates"). Agents allocate their virtual money o=
r rate the goods to indicate their importance or value.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>How does CREA provide a solution to my dispute =
?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        CREA2 provides a solution to your dispute by analyz=
ing the preferences submitted by all agents using advanced AI and game-theo=
retical algorithms. The platform then generates a proposed allocation of go=
ods that aims to satisfy the preferences of all parties involved as fairly =
as possible.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>What happens once all agents agree on the propo=
sed solution ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        Once all agents agree on the proposed solution, CRE=
A2 finalizes the resolution process.
                        A download button becomes available, allowing users=
 to download the report and proof of resolution. This document serves as a =
certified agreement between the parties, ensuring that the resolution is fo=
rmally recognized, since it is based on Smart-contract Blockchain technolog=
y (WP4).
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"mb-8">
            <h3 class=3D"text-xl font-bold mb-4">Assistance during a disput=
e</h3>
            <div class=3D"flex flex-col">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>What is the videoconference feature on CREA ?</=
h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        During a dispute, CREA2 provides you with the possi=
bility to create a videoconference meeting between you, agents and/or media=
tors. To create a meeting, follow these steps:

                        While navigating the dispute process, click on the =
=E2=80=9Cvideoconference=E2=80=9D button at the bottom of your screen.
                        Pick the date and time for the meeting.
                        (Optional) Select a mediator from the mediators=E2=
=80=99 list to join the meeting. You can click on every mediator name if yo=
u need more information.
                        (Optional) Select one or multiple agents to add the=
 meeting.
                        Click on =E2=80=9CSend invitation=E2=80=9D send the=
 meeting request.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>I can't invite an agent to the videoconference.=
 Is this normal ?</h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        Please note that an agent can=E2=80=99t be added to=
 your invitation if they have not joined the dispute and validated the firs=
t step.
                        Once this is done, you will be able to select the a=
gent from the agents=E2=80=99 list.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <hr class=3D"my-4">
                <div class=3D"flex flex-col items-center w-full min-h-[60px=
] justify-center ellipsed-div">
                    <div class=3D"flex w-full justify-between items-center"=
>
                        <h3>How can the chatbot help me during a dispute ?<=
/h3>
                        <button type=3D"button">
                            <i class=3D"fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <p class=3D"w-full text-gray-400 text-sm mx-4">
                        The chatbot on CREA2 is designed to assist you by p=
roviding expert answers to your legal questions throughout the dispute reso=
lution process. Here's how it can help:

                        Legal Guidance: The chatbot can offer explanations =
and advice on various legal matters relevant to your dispute, helping you u=
nderstand your rights and obligations.
                        Procedure Clarification: It can clarify procedural =
steps, ensuring you know what to expect and how to proceed at each stage of=
 the dispute resolution process.
                        Document Assistance: If you need help with legal do=
cuments, the chatbot can provide information on how to prepare and submit t=
hem correctly.
                        Regulation Insights: The chatbot can inform you abo=
ut specific regulations and laws that apply to your dispute, ensuring you a=
re aware of the legal framework governing your case.
                        Terminology Explanation: It can explain complex leg=
al terms and jargon, making it easier for you to comprehend the legal aspec=
ts of your dispute.

                        By providing reliable and accurate legal informatio=
n, the chatbot ensures that you are well-informed and better prepared to na=
vigate the dispute resolution process on CREA2.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>


